.TH nbt_taglen 3 (unknown-date) "mcxedit (unknown-version)"
.SH NAME
nbt_taglen \- gets the length of a given NBT

.SH LIBRARY
libmcx
.RI ( libmcx ,\~ \-lmcx )

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmcx/nbt.h>
.B #include <stdint.h>
.B #include <sys/types.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t nbt_taglen(const uint8_t *" tag ", ssize_t " maxlen ,
.BI "                   int " root ", struct nbt_cache *" cache );

.SH DESCRIPTION
.P
.I tag
is a pointer to the start of the NBT
.P
.I maxlen
is the maximum number of bytes the NBT can be (inclusive).
Must be a value >=0.
.P
.I root
is the current depth we're parsing from, to ensure
.BR NBT_NEST_MAX " is respected."
.RB "Must be a value 0..." NBT_NEST_MAX .
.P
.I cache
TODO: the cache as it stands is broken,
writing a description for this is pointless as it'll change dramatically.

.SH RETURN VALUE
On success,
.B nbt_taglen()
returns the number of bytes that this tag occupies.
On failure, a number <0 is returned, encoding the error as -error.

.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
.RI "we ended up beyond " maxlen .
.TP
.B EINVAL
.IR root " wasn't between"
.RB 0... NBT_NEST_MAX ,
.RI "or this " maxlen " is too large."
.TP
.B EOVERFLOW
The item length for an array or list would result in a negative value.
.TP
.B EMCXTAG
An invalid tag was encountered.
.TP
.B EMCXITER
.RB "The nest limit of " NBT_NEST_MAX " was reached."

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mcx_addkey_end (3),
